Aerie-Purpose: Tell the delegate whether a window with no opener starts as a form sent with POST, and which referrer the page chose, so that "Links open" leaves forms alone and passes the referrer on.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: content/browser/web_contents (web_contents_impl.cc), content/public/browser (BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #141. WebContentsImpl::CreateNewWindow adds a window that the renderer made with no opener (a link or a form
with target=_blank) to a tab strip through the delegate, and only after that starts its load with the referrer and
the POST body of the request. The delegate therefore cannot see either when it decides where the link opens. This
patch sets one user data object, AerieCreatedWindowInfo (overlay,
content/public/browser/aerie_created_window_info.h), on the new contents before the delegate is called: the
referrer of the request and a flag that says the request is a form sent with POST. Nothing else changes. The
header is a new source of //content/public/browser.

--- a/content/public/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/content/public/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
   sources = [
     "active_url_message_filter.cc",
     "active_url_message_filter.h",
+    "aerie_created_window_info.h",
     "allow_service_worker_result.cc",
     "allow_service_worker_result.h",
     "anchor_element_preconnect_delegate.h",
--- a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
@@ -139,6 +139,7 @@
 #include "content/browser/webui/web_ui_impl.h"
 #include "content/common/content_switches_internal.h"
 #include "content/common/features.h"
+#include "content/public/browser/aerie_created_window_info.h"
 #include "content/public/browser/ax_inspect_factory.h"
 #include "content/public/browser/browser_context.h"
 #include "content/public/browser/browser_plugin_guest_manager.h"
@@ -5929,6 +5930,17 @@
     AddWebContentsDestructionObserver(new_contents_impl);
   }
 
+  if (params.opener_suppressed) {
+    // Aerie (issue #141): the load of a window with no opener starts only after
+    // the delegate has added it to a tab strip, so what the delegate needs to
+    // know about it (a form sent with POST, the referrer) is left on the contents.
+    new_contents_impl->SetUserData(
+        &kAerieCreatedWindowInfoKey,
+        std::make_unique<AerieCreatedWindowInfo>(
+            params.referrer.To<Referrer>(),
+            params.form_submission_post_data != nullptr));
+  }
+
